notes: "HUANDENG is built on open work, but the relationships differ. OpenSlide is the editor code foundation under MIT. OpenPPTD contributes only the MathML-to-OMML formula conversion modules, not the whole document model. PptxGenJS generates the PPTX export; Apache ECharts, KaTeX and Font Awesome are dependencies for charts, formulas and icons. PowerPoint and WPS are the file-and-canvas model this project reacts to. Kimi/Moonshot and open-kimi-ppt-skill are where I first met the PPTD approach; this is not a claim that Kimi invented a standard. PPTist, Slidev, Presenton, PPTAgent, PPTMaster, OpenSlides Studio (openslides.dev), OPF and VS Code are workflow inspiration and researched alternatives. HUANDENG is not affiliated with or endorsed by Kimi or the named projects. The not-yet list keeps the talk from implying completeness."
